flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a release reaches the Chrome Web Store
    accDescr: After every release, every day at 00:17 UTC and when started by hand with a tag, the workflow signs in to the Chrome Web Store and asks for the state of the item. A sign-in that Google turns away, a rejected release, a warning, a takedown or a review of more than 7 days fail the run, with the reason and the fix in its summary, and the bot-health sweep of the night keeps an issue open. While a review is pending, the run ends with a note, and a later day delivers the release. When the store has the release already, nothing happens. Otherwise a job without any secret takes the zip of the release and checks its provenance and its version; a release without a zip or a zip without a valid provenance fails the run. It keeps the zip as an artifact, and a job that reaches only Google compares its bytes, uploads it and submits it for review. When the store refuses the submission because the Developer Dashboard lacks something that the version needs, the run fails as well, and names what the release asks for beyond the version of the store. When a review began in the meantime, the run ends with the same note as for a pending review.

    start["After a release, every day at 00:17 UTC,<br>or by hand with a tag"]
    ask["Sign in and ask the store<br>for the state of the item"]
    decide{"What does the store say<br>about the release?"}
    fail["The run fails, with the reason<br>and the fix in its summary"]
    issue["The bot-health sweep of the night<br>keeps an issue open"]
    wait["A note: a review is pending,<br>a later day delivers the release"]
    has["A note: the store has it already"]
    package["Take the zip of the release, check its provenance<br>without any secret, keep it as an artifact"]
    store["Compare its bytes, upload it and submit it,<br>from a job that reaches only Google"]
    review["Google reviews the release<br>and publishes it"]

    start --> ask --> decide
    ask -- "Google turns the sign-in away" --> fail
    decide -- "rejected, warned, taken down,<br>or in review for more than 7 days" --> fail
    decide -- "a review is pending" --> wait
    decide -- "published already" --> has
    decide -- "the store lacks it" --> package --> store --> review
    package -- "no zip, or no valid provenance" --> fail
    store -- "the dashboard lacks something" --> fail
    store -- "a review began in the meantime" --> wait
    fail --> issue

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class ask,package,store bot
    class has,review done
    class fail,issue person
